## 4.10 Western blot analysis
A549 cells were seeded on 6-well plate \( (5\,\times\,10^{5}/\mathrm{well}) \) and incubated in \( 37\,^{\circ}\mathrm{C} \) overnight. The \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8@siRNA} \) \( (30\ \upmu\mathrm{g/mL}) \) was added into the wells. The photo plus group was irradiated laser \( (808\;\mathrm{nm},\,0.75\;\mathrm{W/cm}^{2}) \) for \( 5\;\mathrm{min} \). Then, cells were incubated for another \( 12\;\mathrm{h} \) with fresh medium, harvested for western blotting. The protein abundance in different groups was analyzed by ImageJ \( 2\times \) (2.1.4.7, Rawak Software, Inc).
## 4.11 In vivo studies
When the tumor volume reached \( 100{-}150\;\mathrm{mm}^{3} \) in size, A549 tumor model bearing nude mice were randomly divided into 5 groups \( (n=4) \): (A) PBS, (B) \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8} \), (C) \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8} \) plus laser, (D) \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8@siSur} \), (E) \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8@siSur} \) plus laser. \( 100\;\upmu\mathrm{L} \) \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8@siSur} \) samples (containing \( 90\;\upmu\mathrm{g} \) \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8} \) and \( 9\;\mathrm{pmol} \) siSur) or equivalent \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8} \) were intratumorally injected into the tumor at day 0 and 5. The control groups were injected with an equal volume of PBS. Post injection \( 30\;\mathrm{min} \), the tumor in irradiated group received the laser treatment \( (808\;\mathrm{nm},\,0.75\;\mathrm{W/cm}^{2},\,10\;\mathrm{min}) \). The fluorescent signals of tumor region were recorded by a Caliper IVIS Luminia II multispectral imaging system (PE, USA) using \( 745\;\mathrm{nm} \) as the excitation wavelength, at the time points before and after \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8@siSur} \) injection, and after \( \mathrm{ICG@ZIF-8@siSur} \) injection plus different periods of irradiation. In the 18-days therapy course, the tumor volume and mice body weight were monitored every two days; the volume \( =\,A B^{2}/2 \), where \( A \) and \( B \) are the longer and shorter diameter of the tumor, respectively. Mice were sacrificed at the end of therapy course, major organs including heart, liver, spleen, lung and kidney in each group were harvested and fixed in \( 4\% \) paraformaldehyde, then embedded in paraffin and sectioned for H&E staining. The tissues were observed under digital microscopy (Olympus BX53, Japan).
